## Classic Black and Orange, Reworked for Short Nails

Everyone pictures a full black and orange hand the second Halloween nails come up. On a short nail, that pairing works better in fragments than in full force.

1. **Solid black with one orange spiderweb accent.** Nine nails in matte black, one in a fine orange web over a sheer black base.
2. **Orange base, black French tip.** A thin black tip on a squoval or short square shape reads sharper than a full-colour block.
3. **Black and orange half-moon.** The cuticle line in orange, the rest in black, works especially well on short round nails where a full French would look cramped.
4. **Pumpkin accent nail.** One tiny orange pumpkin with a black stem on a nude or black base, the rest left clean.
5. **Marbled black and orange swirl.** Kept to a single accent nail so the marbling stays visible rather than muddy.

The trick with **short Halloween nails** in this palette is restraint. A full ten-nail black and orange set can look busy on a small canvas, but scaled down to one or two accent nails, the same colours read as intentional rather than costume-like. Anyone wanting the fuller, denser version of this palette across all ten nails should look at <a href='/blog/halloween/black-halloween-nails'>black Halloween nails</a> for sets built specifically around that density.

