## Short Halloween French Tips and Elongating Designs

A French tip does more work on a short nail than almost any other technique on this list. Swap the classic white line for black, blood red, or deep purple, and the same elongating effect that makes a French manicure timeless suddenly reads as Halloween-specific.

A micro French tip in black on a short almond shape tapers the eye toward the tip exactly where the colour sits, making the whole nail look longer in the process. A blood-red tip on a short square nail keeps the geometry sharp while adding just enough colour to feel seasonal. A double French, one thin line in black followed by a thinner line in orange just above it, adds detail without adding bulk. Short coffin nails take this particularly well, since the squared tip already reads longer than a round or squoval shape, and a dark tip amplifies that further. Readers considering the shape itself in more depth can look at <a href='https://mirelleinspo.com/blog/coffin-nails/short-coffin-nails'>how short coffin nails hold their shape and drama at shorter lengths</a> for more detail on why this particular shape reads bold even without added length.

